  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating the sum of all pairwise differences between outcomes of the two lotteries and preferring the one with the more favorable sum. This involves detailed comparison of outcome values across lotteries. However, the individual’s verbal report shows consideration only of the probability of winning (i.e., getting a non-zero amount), not the specific monetary differences between outcomes. The information used by the individual (probabilities of positive outcomes) is unrelated to the information required by the decision reason (outcome values and their pairwise differences). Furthermore, the justification—higher chance to win—is a probability-based heuristic, not a value-based comparison of outcome spreads. There is no indication that the individual computed or considered differences between outcomes of A and B. Therefore, the decision reason was not used. The individual’s reasoning is based on a different criterion entirely.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
}

